<given-names>U</given-names></name><etal/></person-group>:<article-title>Insulin inhibition of platelet-endothelial interaction is mediated by insulin effects on endothelial cells without direct effects on platelets</article-title>.<source><italic>J Thromb Haemost</italic></source><volume>6</volume>:<fpage>856</fpage>&#x02013;<lpage>864</lpage>,<year>2008</year><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">18284601</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B8"><label>8</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Hers</surname><given-names>I</given-names></name></person-group>:<article-title>Insulin-like growth factor-1 potentiates platelet activation via the IRS/PI3Kalpha pathway</article-title>.<source><italic>Blood</italic></source><volume>110</volume>:<fpage>4243</fpage>&#x02013;<lpage>4252</lpage>,<year>2007</year><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17827393</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B9"><label>9</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Algenstaedt</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><name><surname>Antonetti</surname><given-names>DA</given-names></name><name><surname>Yaffe</surname><given-names>MB</given-names></name><etal/></person-group>:<article-title>Insulin receptor substrate proteins create a link between the tyrosine phosphorylation cascade and the Ca<sup>2+</sup>-ATPases in muscle and heart</article-title>.<source><italic>J Biol Chem</italic></source><volume>272</volume>:<fpage>23696</fpage>&#x02013;<lpage>23702</lpage>,<year>1997</year><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9295312</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B10"><label>10</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Ferreira</surname><given-names>IA</given-names></name><name><surname>Eybrechts</surname><given-names>KL</given-names></name><name><surname>Mocking</surname><given-names>AI</given-names></name><etal/></person-group>:<article-title>IRS-1 mediates inhibition o